# Cloudflare static-assets redirects. Format: <source> <destination> <status>.
# `*` in the source is a splat; `:splat` in the destination reuses it.
# First-match wins, so more-specific rules go above the splat.

# Apple Silicon: `uname -m` on M-series Macs returns `arm64`, but our release
# asset uses the Rust-triple `aarch64`. Alias so the install command on the
# website resolves correctly without touching CI naming.
/unpin-arm64-darwin  https://github.com/unpins/unpin/releases/latest/download/unpin-aarch64-darwin  302

# `unpin` CLI binary downloads → latest GitHub release asset.
/unpin-*  https://github.com/unpins/unpin/releases/latest/download/unpin-:splat  302
